# app.veridian-aios.com -- Cloudflare Pages response headers.
# WO-DPDP-012 §2 for the private prefix, §1 for everything.
#
# How Cloudflare applies this file (its own docs): a request inherits the
# headers of EVERY rule whose pattern matches, in file order, and a header
# name attached twice is comma-joined. So the private rule must first
# DETACH ("! Name") the site-wide Referrer-Policy, in its own rule, before
# a second rule sets the stricter one -- otherwise /app/ would be sent
# "strict-origin-when-cross-origin, no-referrer". src/lib/public-surface.test.ts
# and scripts/check-public-surface.mjs model exactly these merge rules and
# pin the outcome for /app/, /app/index.html and every public page.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/app/*
  ! Referrer-Policy

/app/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Cache-Control: no-store
